{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7707","id":5211801813,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNqXI1Q","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7707","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7707.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7707.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7707","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7707/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7707/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7707/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/304d4f557ce0c2fbfe385468a0e0c569e3ea116a","number":7707,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"docs(atlas): staging-shard ingest gate design (#6057)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Design record for #6057 (Follow-up 38, Cluster 7; parent #6018).\n\n## What this adds\n\n`doc/2026-11-08T13-45-00Z_design_atlas_staging_shard_ingest_gate/` — the gate design the issue asks for:\n\n- **Stage contracts for all five stages** (write, classify, dedup, provenance-check, publish), each as a pure function of the batch returning `(verdict, reason_codes, counts, artifacts)`.\n- **Per-stage pass/fail semantics** in one table (§4), including what `skip` means (never a pass, never bumps a snapshot id) and the fail-closed rule that no verdict = not passed.\n- **Failure/quarantine handling** (§5): quarantine is a state not a deletion; retry resumes at the failing stage; landing is content-addressed so retry is safe; long-lived epic units promote in increments; three-strikes escalation to stop auto-retrying a deterministic failure (spend guardrail, #6018 S3).\n- **Publish atomicity against fan-out search** (§6): the reader-visible invariant, the per-snapshot visibility contract, and the honest position that the indefinite Durable Object cache (#6788) is a known staleness window until #6805 lands rather than something the gate can claim atomic.\n\n## Packet staleness handled\n\nThe packet names #5755 as an open atomicity constraint. #5755 is **CLOSED (2026-11-07)**; its surface moved to #6662/#6664/#6665/#6666 and successor #6788 (+ eviction follow-up #6805). §6 addresses atomicity against those successors, not the closed issue.\n\n## Sibling decisions consumed, not re-decided\n\n#6026 (versioning — landed design), #3125 (keep-all, occurrences), #5733 (dedup findings are data), #5669 (staging tier, ≤500-row bound, merge-on-close). The three obligations this note adds that those designs did not state (per-row tier split at publish, snapshot-id-in-manifest, three-strikes quarantine bound) are called out explicitly in §7 as gate requirements to reflect back, not as changes to their decisions.\n\n## Follow-ons\n\n§9 splits implementation into six follow-ons. The gate-record state machine is tracked as #7709 against #5669; remaining follow-ons are filed against their siblings as those designs land.\n\nDesign only — no implementation.\n\nRefs #6057\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796737329&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7707&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7707&signature=bec22265ce23bee5db4adfe40ab7d232a9c36345b62a3792e28cf37c027e923c\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7707?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T13:42:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T10:58:23Z","closed_at":"2026-11-16T10:57:47Z","merged_at":"2026-11-16T10:57:47Z","merge_commit_sha":"f420d7e95a853ef860b055536cc87737c1a8bb61","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_ur